cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness, please cite it."
title: >-
  attachment-differ: Cross-Extractor Content Divergence as an Evasion Primitive
  in Email Attachment Pipelines
abstract: >-
  A differential-testing harness that measures where multiple production content
  extractors (Tika, PDFBox, pypdf, pdfminer, oletools) diverge on the same
  attachment and from an OCR render-oracle, with a vector taxonomy, a
  detector-impact (evasion) study, and a re-implementation of PDF Mirage's
  font-verification defense showing it does not generalize to non-font vectors.
authors:
  - given-names: Ankitha
    family-names: Kundhuru
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"       # update at arXiv/release
license: MIT
keywords:
  - parser differential
  - content extraction
  - email attachment security
  - evasion
  - PDF
  - fuzzing
repository-code: "https://github.com/akundhuru/attachment-differ"
